# Lazy simulators (build memory)

Fundamentals builds OOM during SSG when MDX files **directly import** heavy interactive components. Keep simulators browser-only and lazy.

## In lesson MDX

- Do **not** add `import FooSimulator from "@site/src/components/interactive/..."`.
- Use the component tag directly in JSX: `<FooSimulator />`.
- Global registration lives in `src/theme/MDXComponents.js` via `lazySimulators`.

## Adding a new simulator

1. Create `src/components/interactive/MyTopicSimulator.js`.
2. Register it in `src/components/interactive/lazySimulators.js` (or regenerate that file from the folder listing).
3. Use `<MyTopicSimulator />` in MDX — no import line.

## Why

Direct imports pull every simulator into the server/webpack graph at build time. `lazyMdxComponent()` (`BrowserOnly` + `React.lazy`) defers loading to the client and keeps SSG memory bounded.

## Same pattern for other heavy MDX widgets

Prefer `lazyMdxComponent()` in `MDXComponents.js` for `PistonRunner`, `CodeExercise`, challenges, etc. New heavy widgets should follow this pattern by default.
